{
  "sources": "OPUS target-centered Sun/observer coordinates and range (checked against phase and pixel scale). Original PDS Galileo SSI NORTH_AZIMUTH clockwise from image right, converted by +90 degrees to image up. OPUS positions/roll are not used: they mismatch the raw image. Earlier PDS label Sun/range fields also disagree with recorded phase and pixel scale, so are not used.",
  "method": "Only image-center translation is fitted to the apparent illuminated ellipsoid; fixed dimensions, body axes and source Sun/observer geometry. Sky median is subtracted before empirical bounded lunar-Lambert normalization of relative DN.",
  "limits": "Original eight-bit reconstructed SSI counts, not radiometrically calibrated I/F. Smooth ellipsoid and approximate pointing limit registration, especially for images only 5 to 20 pixels across. Original phase and cast shadows cannot be recovered where source signal is absent.",
